ty and the DNA double-stranded break connection.</article-title><source>Nat Rev Genet</source><volume>2(3)</volume><fpage>196</fpage><lpage>206</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11256071</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004805-Wyman1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wyman</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanaar</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>DNA double-strand break repair: All's well that ends well.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Genet</source><volume>40</volume><fpage>363</fpage><lpage>383</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16895466</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004805-Mitelman3"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitelman</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Mertens</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Prevalence estimates of recurrent balanced cytogenetic aberrations and gene fusions in unselected patients with neoplastic disorders.</article-title><source>Genes Chromosomes Cancer</source><volume>43(4)</volume><fpage>350</fpage><lpage>366</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15880352</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004805-Aplan2"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aplan</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Chromosomal translocations involving the MLL gene: Molecular mechanisms.</article-title><source>DNA Repair (Amst)</source><volume>5(9&#x02013;10)</volume><fpage>1265</fpage><lpage>1272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16797254</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004805-Felix1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group pe